WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.907
Police and Emergencies.

2
00:00:02.187 --> 00:00:06.475
Day 54 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:09.249
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.529 --> 00:00:18.703
Today's goal: stay clear and calm in an emergency: call for help, report a theft or accident, and answer police questions with exact facts.

5
00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:20.970
Watch out:

6
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.957
Emergency numbers (India).

7
00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:33.711
112 all emergencies, 100 police, 101 fire, 108 ambulance (most states), 1930 cyber-fraud helpline.

8
00:00:33.991 --> 00:00:42.311
Abroad, check the local number before you travel (911 US, 112 EU, 999 UK).

9
00:00:43.661 --> 00:00:44.515
Part 1.

10
00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:46.523
The emergency call formula.

11
00:00:47.773 --> 00:00:48.711
You could say:

12
00:00:48.991 --> 00:00:50.549
There's been a road accident.

13
00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:57.037
A bike and a car have collided on Outer Ring Road, near the Marathahalli bridge, opposite the petrol pump.

14
00:00:57.317 --> 00:01:00.175
One man is bleeding from the head and isn't moving.

15
00:01:00.455 --> 00:01:07.303
My name is Ashish, and my number is 98450 12345.

16
00:01:08.653 --> 00:01:09.528
Part 2.

17
00:01:09.808 --> 00:01:10.768
Key words.

18
00:01:12.018 --> 00:01:13.362
Here is a quick table:

19
00:01:13.642 --> 00:01:15.263
Word or phrase, and Meaning.

20
00:01:15.543 --> 00:01:38.413
FIR or complaint or report: the official police record. theft or stolen or pickpocketed or snatched: taking your things. accident or collision or hit-and-run: road incidents. witness: someone who saw it. fraud or scam or OTP or unauthorised transaction: online crime. injured or unconscious or bleeding: medical state.

21
00:01:39.763 --> 00:01:40.659
Part 3.

22
00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:42.304
Questions you'll be asked.

23
00:01:43.554 --> 00:01:44.898
Here is a quick table:

24
00:01:45.178 --> 00:01:46.949
Police ask, and You answer.

25
00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:48.167
What happened?:

26
00:01:48.447 --> 00:01:50.730
My phone was snatched by two men on a bike.

27
00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:51.949
When and where?:

28
00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:57.434
About 8:30 pm today, outside the Indiranagar metro station, exit B.

29
00:01:57.714 --> 00:01:58.909
Can you describe them?:

30
00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:01.557
Two young men, black helmets, a red bike.

31
00:02:01.837 --> 00:02:03.351
I couldn't see the number plate.

32
00:02:03.631 --> 00:02:04.698
What was stolen?:

33
00:02:04.978 --> 00:02:07.090
An iPhone 14, black cover.

34
00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.247
Here's the IMEI number from the box.

35
00:02:09.527 --> 00:02:10.893
Were there any witnesses?:

36
00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:12.517
A shopkeeper saw it.

37
00:02:12.797 --> 00:02:13.842
He's still there.

38
00:02:15.192 --> 00:02:16.109
Part 4.

39
00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:17.605
Questions you'll ask.

40
00:02:18.855 --> 00:02:21.117
How do I file an FIR or complaint?

41
00:02:21.397 --> 00:02:22.826
Can I file it online?

42
00:02:23.106 --> 00:02:26.007
Could I have a copy of the complaint or FIR number?

43
00:02:26.287 --> 00:02:27.589
What should I do next?

44
00:02:27.869 --> 00:02:29.917
(block SIM, inform bank).

45
00:02:30.197 --> 00:02:32.223
Will you inform me if you find anything?

46
00:02:33.573 --> 00:02:34.533
Part 5.

47
00:02:34.813 --> 00:02:37.544
Conversation 1: reporting a stolen phone.

48
00:02:38.794 --> 00:02:40.821
Here is how the conversation goes.

49
00:02:41.101 --> 00:02:42.594
Yes, what's the problem?

50
00:02:42.874 --> 00:02:44.687
I'd like to report a theft.

51
00:02:44.967 --> 00:02:47.335
My phone was snatched about an hour ago.

52
00:02:47.615 --> 00:02:48.853
Where did it happen?

53
00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:54.082
Outside Indiranagar metro station, exit B, at around 8:30.

54
00:02:54.362 --> 00:02:55.791
Did you see the person?

55
00:02:57.141 --> 00:02:58.741
The conversation continues.

56
00:02:59.021 --> 00:03:00.792
Two men on a red bike.

57
00:03:01.072 --> 00:03:02.651
Both wore black helmets.

58
00:03:02.931 --> 00:03:04.040
Okay.

59
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.496
Which phone, and do you have the IMEI number?

60
00:03:06.776 --> 00:03:08.525
An iPhone 14.

61
00:03:08.805 --> 00:03:10.597
Here's the IMEI from the bill.

62
00:03:10.877 --> 00:03:13.053
I've already blocked my SIM.

63
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:14.080
Good.

64
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.683
Fill in this form.

65
00:03:15.963 --> 00:03:17.584
We'll register the complaint.

66
00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.534
The conversation continues.

67
00:03:20.814 --> 00:03:23.289
Could I have a copy with the complaint number?

68
00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.339
I need it for insurance.

69
00:03:25.619 --> 00:03:27.091
Yes, you'll get a copy.

70
00:03:27.371 --> 00:03:28.523
Thank you, sir.

71
00:03:29.873 --> 00:03:30.812
Part 6.

72
00:03:31.092 --> 00:03:33.375
Conversation 2: online fraud.

73
00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:36.651
Here is how the conversation goes.

74
00:03:36.931 --> 00:03:39.363
Hello, is this the cyber-fraud helpline?

75
00:03:39.643 --> 00:03:43.142
Money was taken from my account without my permission.

76
00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:44.766
How much, and when?

77
00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:48.694
25,000, rupeesabout twenty minutes ago.

78
00:03:48.974 --> 00:03:54.115
I got a call from someone pretending to be from my bank, and I shared an OTP.

79
00:03:54.395 --> 00:03:56.315
I realise now it was a scam.

80
00:03:56.595 --> 00:03:58.217
Have you informed your bank?

81
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.167
The conversation continues.

82
00:04:01.447 --> 00:04:02.428
Not yet.

83
00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.116
I called you first.

84
00:04:04.396 --> 00:04:06.849
Call your bank right away and block your card.

85
00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:09.049
I'm registering your complaint now.

86
00:04:09.329 --> 00:04:11.079
What's the transaction ID?

87
00:04:11.359 --> 00:04:20.148
It's UPI ref 6102 9933 4471.

88
00:04:20.428 --> 00:04:24.545
Your complaint number is CYB-77120.

89
00:04:24.825 --> 00:04:27.833
Please also file a report on the cybercrime portal.

90
00:04:29.183 --> 00:04:30.783
The conversation continues.

91
00:04:31.063 --> 00:04:32.002
Thank you.

92
00:04:32.282 --> 00:04:33.818
I'll call the bank now.

93
00:04:35.168 --> 00:04:36.107
Part 7.

94
00:04:36.387 --> 00:04:38.349
Stay calm: phrases that help.

95
00:04:39.599 --> 00:04:41.050
Please send help quickly.

96
00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:42.397
The address is...

97
00:04:42.677 --> 00:04:43.957
I'll stay on the line.

98
00:04:44.237 --> 00:04:47.607
Is there anything I should do until the ambulance arrives?

99
00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.466
Sorry, could you repeat that?

100
00:04:49.746 --> 00:04:50.855
I'm a bit shaken.

101
00:04:52.205 --> 00:04:53.080
Part 8.

102
00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.405
Speak today.

103
00:04:55.655 --> 00:05:01.159
Save 112, your local police station and your bank's card-block number in your phone.

104
00:05:01.439 --> 00:05:05.706
Practise the emergency call formula with your home address and a landmark.

105
00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:08.592
That's the end of this lesson.

106
00:05:08.872 --> 00:05:13.523
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

107
00:05:13.803 --> 00:05:19.925
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

